==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/soː/|[s̪oə̯]}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-så.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|sv|non|svá}}, from {{der|sv|gem-pro|*swa}}, {{m|gem-pro|*swē}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|sv|adverb}}

# [[so]], like that, in such a way
#: {{ux|sv|Är det inte '''så'''?|Isn't it '''so'''?}}
#: {{ux|sv|en '''så''' kallad skruvboll|a '''so'''-called curve ball}}
#: {{ux|sv|Kolla hur jag hoppar och hoppa '''(så)''' som jag gör|Look at how I jump and jump like me ("jump '''(in such a way)''' as I do" – the ''så'' is redundant)}}
# [[so]], [[alright]] (to indicate that something is finished)
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''', maten är klar!|'''So''', the food is done!}}
# [[so]] (to such a degree)
#: {{ux|sv|Jag trodde inte den var '''så''' stor.|I didn't think it was '''so''' big.}}
#: {{ux|sv|Den är '''så''' stor att den inte får plats.|It is '''so''' big that it doesn't fit.}}
# [[so]] (after {{m|sv|inte||not}})
#: {{ux|sv|inte '''så''' bra|not '''so''' good}}
# {{ng|An optional filler, after for example {{m|sv|rätt}} and {{m|sv|ganska}} – compare "not so" in English.}}
#: {{ux|sv|ganska/rätt '''(så)''' stor|pretty big}}
#: {{ux|sv|ganska/rätt '''(så)''' liten|pretty small}}
# [[then]] (under such circumstances)
#: {{ux|sv|Om man köper pizza '''så''' blir man glad|If you buy pizza, '''then''' you become happy}}
# [[so]] (as a consequence)
#: {{ux|sv|Det regnade, '''så''' han blev blöt|It rained, '''so''' he got wet}}
# [[so]] (before a conclusion)
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''' det kan inte varit han som gjorde det|'''So''' it can't have been him who did it}}
# [[so]] (very), [[how]] (very), what a
#: {{ux|sv|Kaninen är '''så''' söt!|The rabbit is '''so''' cute!}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''' roligt!|'''How''' nice!}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''' trevligt att ni kunde komma!|'''How''' nice that you could come!}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''' stor han har blivit!|He's grown! ("'''How''' big he has become!")}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''' tråkigt!|'''How''' sad!}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Så''' synd!|'''What a''' pity!}}
# [[even]] (if)
#: {{ux|sv|'''Om jag så''' får en miljon så gör jag det inte|'''Even if I''' ("If I so") get a million bucks, I'm not doing it}}
# [[as]] (when synonymous with ''so'')
#: {{ux|sv|'''så''' vitt jag vet|'''as/so''' far as I know}}
# {{lb|sv|uncommon}} [[then]], [[thereafter]]
#: {{syn|sv|sedan|q=more common}}
#: {{ux|sv|Se först åt vänster, '''så''' åt höger.|First look to the left, '''then''' to the right.}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|sv|conjunction}}

# [[so]], [[that]]
#: {{ux|sv|Vi måste åka '''så''' att vi hinner hem i tid|We have to go '''so''' that we make it home in time}}
#: {{ux|sv|Stäng av plattan '''så att inte''' maten bränns|Turn off the plate '''so''' the food '''doesn't''' burn ("så att inte" {{=}} "so that not" {{=}} "lest," but with a more everyday tone)}}
#: {{ux|sv|Det regnade, '''så''' vi satte oss inomhus|It rained, '''so''' we took a table indoors}}
# {{senseid|sv|adverbial filler}} {{ng|Optionally appears between an initial adverbial and the principal verb of a sentence (where a comma would go in English). Compare English "then" for grammatical intuition (though the "så" doesn't carry any meaning or connotations). Note that due to V2 word order, the principal verb follows the adverbial, giving a different word order from English.}}
#: {{ux|sv|Imorgon ('''så''') ska vi äta glass|Tomorrow''',''' we're going to eat ice cream}}
#: {{ux|sv|Om ni kommit tidigare ('''så''') hade ni fått mat|If you had come here earlier''',''' you would've gotten food}}
#: {{ux|sv|Hade det inte regnat så förbaskat ('''så''') hade vi kunnat gå på en promenad|If it hadn't been so darn rainy''',''' we could've gone for a walk}}
#: {{ux|sv|I skogen ('''så''') bodde det en trollkarl|In the forest''',''' there lived a wizard}}

=====Usage notes=====
Only used for initial adverbials in ({{senseno|sv|adverbial filler}}). "Vi ska äta glass imorgon så" is ungrammatical (or means "We're going to eat ice cream tomorrow in such a way").

====Pronoun====
{{head|sv|pronoun}}

# [[such]], [[that]]
#: {{ux|sv|i '''så''' fall|in '''that''' case, if so}}

